  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Find the differential $\\text{d}f$ for the function $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz).$",
  "worked_solution": "We compute the differential using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y,z) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{∂f}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\frac{yz\\,\\text{d}x}{xyz}+\\frac{xz\\,\\text{d}y}{xyz}+\\frac{xy\\,\\text{d}z}{xyz} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\,\\text{d}x}{x}+\\frac{\\,\\text{d}y}{y}+\\frac{\\,\\text{d}z}{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
